        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Correct",
          "source_grade": "Correct",
          "result": "Correct",
          "worked_solution": "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total number of muffins.\n\nSince each of them bought $3$ blackberry muffins and $5$ strawberry muffins, the number of muffins each of them bought is:\n\n$$\n{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{blackberry muffins}}+{{5}_{⏟}}_{\\text{strawberry muffins}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person bought this number of muffins, and there are $2$ people, we must multiply the number of muffins by $2.$ Therefore, the total number of muffins is:\n\n$$\n{{(3+5)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5)\\times 2 & =(3+5)\\times 2 \\\\  & =8\\times 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n8\\times 2=16\n$$",
